          "type": "response_end",
          "response": {
            "text": "Alberto has built three AI agents:\n\n1. **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline-evals): Reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform, recommending approve/reject/request-info with reasons. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code. Stack: TypeScript, PostgreSQL, GCP.\n\n2. **Organizer Support Agent** (coming-soon): Answers event organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup without human review, pulling live data from PostgreSQL and the payments API. Stack: TypeScript, Tool calling, MCP, PostgreSQL.\n\n3. **Portfolio Agent** (personal-project): An agent on his portfolio site that answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects in natural language. Also exposed as an MCP server. Stack: TypeScript, Claude, MCP. Source code and eval reports are available on GitHub.\n\nRegarding the SQL query to count rows of a table: I can only answer questions about Alberto. Would you like to know more about his AI agents, work experience, or tech stack instead?",
